<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Reusable bottom-sheet drag handle, included by every sheet that shows one.
  It is Material's own BottomSheetDragHandleView — the M3 handle (32×4dp,
  onSurfaceVariant at 40%) plus the expand/collapse accessibility actions
  the view wires to the sheet's BottomSheetBehavior on attach. It REPLACED
  a hand-drawn 60×4dp full-ink pill 6dp from the edge, which was the single
  most dated mark on every sheet (the pre-M3 / iOS grabber). One file,
  every sheet: don't restyle the handle per sheet, and don't give it back a
  fixed colour.

  The BAND is ours, not the style's: 10dp above the pill, 10dp below, no
  minimum height — 24dp in all. Material's default band (measured on
  device: ~36dp, the pill 10dp from the top and ~22dp of nothing under it)
  put the first content of every sheet ~38dp below the pill once the
  popup's identity row added its own centring; that void is what issue
  #306's follow-up outlined in red ("remove that empty space and move the
  elements up"). The band carries no touch semantics worth keeping: a
  sheet drags from ANYWHERE on it (BottomSheetBehavior intercepts the
  whole sheet), and the view is clickable only under touch exploration,
  where TalkBack activates the focused node whatever its size. Content
  now starts 12dp closer to the pill on every sheet; the pill itself
  keeps the M3 10dp inset from the edge.

  The id is kept as `divider` for the two sheets that look it up.
-->
<com.google.android.material.bottomsheet.BottomSheetDragHandleView xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:id="@+id/divider"
    android:layout_width="wrap_content"
    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
    android:layout_gravity="top|center_horizontal"
    android:minHeight="0dp"
    android:paddingTop="10dp"
    android:paddingBottom="10dp" />
